{"hookSpecificOutput":{"hookEventName":"PreToolUse","permissionDecision":"deny","permissionDecisionReason":"Atelier full-autonomy contract: pipeline p1 is mid-autonomous execution at phase 'execute' (status running, awaiting 'workflow'). You may NOT ask the user — there is no human in the loop after Brainstorm. Almost always the right move is to DECIDE IT YOURSELF: take the sensible default (the most reasonable, reversible, convention-matching choice) and keep driving — a question you were about to ask is a decision you should make. If a fan-out just returned (awaiting is still 'workflow'), process its result autonomously: on a review's findings — however large or architectural — dispatch the fix to MEET THE SPEC/PLAN, because the spec is the contract; build exactly what it requires and do NOT ask the user to set, confirm, or lower the acceptance bar — then set awaiting:null and continue. status:\"failed\" is the LAST RESORT, only when you LEGITIMATELY CANNOT ADVANCE: a genuine hard blocker with no workable default — e.g. a required credential that is truly absent and nothing can substitute (it should have been captured in the spec's 'Prerequisites / Required Access' section during speccing). Only in that case write failure:{stage,reason,lastError} naming the blocker to @ROOT@/.atelier/pipelines/p1/state.json and stop. Do NOT fail for anything a sensible default would carry. A decision only the owner can make goes into a gate file (gates/<id>.md, VERDICT/SIGNED left blank) and the flow continues on everything it does not block. (If this genuinely IS the Brainstorm phase, you forgot to set awaiting:\"user\" in state.json first — set it, then ask.)"}}

exit=0
